  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-VNM127</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reformed labour market institutions are used for improving labour standards for all  workers and formalizing informal employment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Viet Nam, nearly seven in ten workers are informal, with the highest rate in agriculture.  The country&#x2019;s Socio-Economic Development Strategy 2021-2030 recognizes informality as a hindrance to inclusive growth. In this biennium, the focus has been on the development of a government-owned information base on informality that serves by informing national policy dialogues.
ILO technical support aims at promoting a comprehensive and integrated approach to formalization and strengthening the capacity of the tripartite-plus group on informality, and targeting informal workers, particularly women in sectors facing greater challenges in transitioning to decent work.</narrative>
  </description>
